Now we need to check that we didn't use any action that requires route_sequence_context_set false when it's true, etc. We never set route_sequence_context_set (we used nominal clearance which does not set it). So it stays false. Then we used finalize_candidate_direct (step39) requires not route_sequence_context_set shift_candidate_alpha (true). Good. After step39 we don't use route_sequence_context_set again. So fine.

Similarly for beta.

Now we need to check that we didn't use any action that requires candidate_finalized false when it's true, etc. We used finalize_candidate_direct (step39) requires not candidate_finalized shift_candidate_alpha (false at that time). After step39 candidate_finalized becomes true. Then we used allocate_dispatch_slot_for_candidate (step40) does not require candidate_finalized. Then execute_schedule_dispatch (step41) requires not dispatched shift_candidate_alpha (true). No action requires candidate_finalized false later. So fine.

Similarly for beta.

Now we need to check that we didn't use any action that requires dispatched false when it's true, etc. We used execute_*_dispatch actions which require not dispatched. After they execute, dispatched becomes true. No further actions require dispatched false for those entities. So fine.

Now we need to check that we didn't use any action that requires dispatch_allocated false when it's true, etc. We used allocate_dispatch_slot_for_candidate which requires not dispatch_allocated. After allocation, dispatch_allocated becomes true. Then we used execute_*_dispatch which requires dispatch_allocated true. After execution, dispatch_allocated is not affected (remains true). No further actions require dispatch_allocated false for those entities. So fine.

Now we need to check that we didn't use any action that requires dispatch_slot_available false when it's true, etc. We used allocate_dispatch_slot_for_candidate which requires dispatch_slot_available. After allocation, dispatch_slot_available becomes false. Then we used execute_*_dispatch which releases dispatch_slot_available (makes it true). So after each execute, dispatch_slot_available becomes true again. Good.

Now we need to check that we didn't use any action that requires vehicle_available false when it's true, etc. We used allocate_vehicle_unit which requires vehicle_available. After allocation, vehicle_available becomes false. Then we used execute_*_dispatch which releases vehicle_available (makes it true). So after each execute, vehicle becomes available again. Good.

Now we need to check that we didn't use any action that requires operator_available false when it's true, etc. We used assign_operator_resource which requires operator_available. After assignment, operator_available becomes false. Then we used release_operator_resource which requires candidate_operator_linked (true) and makes operator_available true. So after each release, operator becomes available again. Good.

Now we need to check that we didn't use any action that requires skill_certificate_available false when it's true, etc. We used assign_skill_certificate which requires skill_certificate_available. After assignment, skill_certificate_available becomes false. Then we used release_skill_certificate which requires candidate_skill_certificate_linked (true) and makes skill_certificate_available true. So after each release, skill certificate becomes available again. Good.

